  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nLatest radar (as of early this afternoon) places portrays\nshowers across the western half of the area, although dry air \nnear the surface will likely prevent the vast majority of the \nprecipitation from reaching the surface. Nonetheless, some very \nlight rain showers may periodically occur west of I-71 through \nearly this evening so have introduced slight chance PoPs for the\nnext several hours. Otherwise, Halloween will remain dry and \nmostly cloudy with temperatures generally falling into the 40s \nand lower 50s tonight. The only exception will be mid to upper \n30s across interior eastern Crawford/Erie counties in PA. High \npressure will gradually shift east through the rest of the \nweekend and early next week, providing dry weather and gradually\nincreasing temperatures through Tuesday. Tuesday will likely be\nthe warmest day of the week with high temperatures in the 70s \nexpected.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\nA pattern shift is expected for mid to late week as the\naforementioned high shifts east and a low pressure system\napproaches from the west. Showers may sneak into northwestern\nzones as early as late Tuesday, but guidance generally favors\ndry weather until the low's accompanying cold front nears the\nlocal area early Wednesday. From there, periodic showers are\nlikely as the front crosses the CWA through Thursday with\nadditional scattered showers possible as a secondary cold front\nmoves through on Friday. As far as temperatures go, temps in the\n70s will likely continue into Wednesday before dropping back\ninto the 60s for the end of the week.",
